    "description": "Mineral and Gemstone Collection Lot\nVintage Geological Specimens\nMulti-Colored, Various Minerals, 20th Century\nA diverse and extensive collection of geological specimens, fossils, and minerals. This lot includes a wide variety of raw and polished materials, spanning from common minerals to paleontological fossils, curated for educational study, lapidary use, or private display.\nItems Included:\nNatural Gemstone Collection: \"Jewels in the Rough\" 21-specimen display case\nTrilobite Fossil: Peronopsis Interstrictus specimen in an individual protective case\nPyrite Specimens: Multiple large raw crystalline clusters with metallic luster\nMounted Minerals: Approximately 30 specimens on identification cards (includes Beryl, Agate, Iron Ore, and Jasper)\nSea Glass & Pottery: Assorted weathered fragments and historical pottery shards\nLoose Gemstones: Large lot of tumbled and raw stones including Rose Quartz and Amethyst\nCondition:\nGood vintage condition. Specimens are largely intact and securely attached to identification cards where applicable. Cards show minor age-related toning. Plastic display cases exhibit light shelf wear but remain functional. Natural variations and geological textures are present across all samples.\nWarehouse Location: Cleveland\nDue to our lighting, white glare lines may appear on items - This is NOT damage\nIf you have any questions regarding the quality or authenticity of this item or general questions regarding and item, please click Contact Seller on the item page and send us a message. We are available to answer your questions Monday through Friday, 8 am - 3:00 pm, EST.\n* For combined shipping policy see the shipping tab.\nSome items may contain unseen flaws not noted in the description.\nSee Photos. Items sold as-is.",
